 | done | `./zn done R0010` | requires `./zn trace R0010 --check` to pass for the commit it lands and the final review (`final-review-NNN.md`; `review-NNN.md` is for the per-layer code review only and cannot stand in) to be resolved (verdict `approve`, or every open finding — each finding answered `fixed <sha>: <what>; consequences: <what the fix could break, and how that was checked, or none>`, `refuted`, or, for a medium or low finding and only as zz-execute Phase 4 step 7 allows, `deferred <id>: <why>` naming a backlog issue — ruled by the human in `## Open to the human`) and the raft's `check.sh` to pass. Refuses a member whose approval no longer matches the contract (the design sections, the acceptance specs and `check.sh`); a member with no approval is not sent back. The checkout must be the published top-layer commit; a lower layer or a top layer behind origin is refused, naming the layer and both shas. Refuses a layer that is not finished, not stacked on the one below, or whose contract changed. Refuses when `./zn trace R0010 --check` fails (missing, failing or stale `trace.md`) or when `final-review-NNN.md` is missing or has no `Verdict:` line. Merges that commit with `--no-ff`, promotes acceptance specs, moves the items to `done/`, runs the affected gate (`z-nile/check.sh --affected`) on that tree. A failing gate rolls the tree back by itself. Inside a spec run it skips the gate, says so, and checks only the promoted specs, and commits one binding commit (`<raft>: bind <id>, <id>`, the final review's `Verdict: <word>`, and `Trace: <done-raft-dir>/trace.md`). Then `gh pr view <n> --json baseRefName -q .baseRefName` and `gh pr edit <n> --base main` for each layer, and `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/main`. A failing gate or a failed retarget rolls back and does not push. A failed push puts each pull request's base back and rolls the tree back. |
 
